  "narrative": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Logic of Experimentation: Rethinking Music Performance Through Artistic Research (2018), published by Leuven University Press, has been cited 5 times. Beyond that, it has been downloaded 5,095 times.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Logic of Experimentation: Rethinking Music Performance Through Artistic Research by Paulo De Assis was published by Leuven University Press in 2018. It is part of the MODID-19febebe56a:Leuven University Press series. Conceptually, the work connects to Computer science, Visual arts and Art.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">OpenAlex records 5 citations. Citations peaked in 2021 with 2 citing works. Notable citing venues include Quodlibet: revista de especializaci\u00f3n musical, CINECA IRIS Institutial research information system (University of Pisa) and twentieth-century music. The citing works include 4 journal articles and 1 book. They come from 4 countries, led by Belgium, the United Kingdom and Portugal.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">It has been downloaded 5,095 times via OAPEN. The work was funded by European Research Council.</p>",
